  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN205.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṉ piriviṉkaṇ vēṟupaṭṭa talaivi vaṟpuṟakkun tōḻikkuc colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the confidante said who was consoling HER who had undergone changes during the separation from HIM.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN205.1">
        <l><anchor n="1"/>uyirkalan toṉṟiya toṉṟupaṭu naṭpiṟ</l>
        <l>ceyirtīr neñcamoṭu ceṟintōr pōlat</l>
        <l>taiya ṉiṉvayiṟ piriyalam yāmeṉap </l>
        <l>poyva luḷḷamoṭu purivuṇak kūṟit</l>
        <l>tuṇi<supplied>vi</supplied>l koḷkaiya rāki yiṉiyē</l>
        <l>nōymali varuttamoṭu <supplied>nuta</supplied>lpacap pūra</l>
        <l>nāma<supplied>ḻa</supplied>t tuṟantaṉa rāyiṉun tāmē</l>
        <l>vāymoḻi nilaiiya cēṇviḷaṅku nallicai</l>
        <l>va<supplied>ḷa</supplied>ṅkeḻu kōcar viḷaṅkupa<supplied>ṭai</supplied> nūṟi</l>
        <l>nilaṅkoḷa veḵkiya polampūṭ kiḷḷi</l>
        <l>pūviri neṭuṅkaḻi nāppaṭ perumpeyark</l>
        <l>kāvirip paṭappaip paṭṭiṉat taṉṉa</l>
        <l>ceḻunakar nalvirun tayarmā rēmuṟa</l>
        <l><supplied>viḻu</supplied>niti yeḷitaṉi ṉeytuka tilla</l>
        <l>maḻaikā lacci<supplied>ra</supplied>ttu māliru ṇīṅki</l>
        <l>nīṭamai nivanta niḻalpaṭu cilampiṟ</l>
        <l>kaṭāa yāṉaik kavuṇmaruṅ ku<supplied>ṟaḻa</supplied></l>
        <l>vāmūr piṟaḻiyuṅ kāmar ceṉṉip</l>
        <l>puliyuri variyataḷ kaṭuppak kaliciṟantu </l>
        <l>nāṭpū vēṅkai naṟumala rutira</l>
        <l>mēkkeḻu peruñciṉai <anchor n="2"/>yēṟik kaṇakkalai</l>
        <l>kūppiṭu vukaḷuṅ kuṉṟakac ciṟuneṟik</l>
        <l>kaṟpiṟaṅ kāriṭai vilaṅkiya </l>
        <l>coṟpeyar tēetta curaṉiṟan tōrē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="2">“Like those who are close, with flawless hearts,</l>
        <l corresp="1">in an intimacy that happened of old in which [they] became one after [their] souls mingled,</l>
        <l corresp="3">woman, we will not separate from you”,</l>
        <l corresp="4">although, talking thus when consumed by desire, with a mind capable of lying,</l>
        <l corresp="5">being one with principles without steadiness, now,</l>
        <l corresp="6">so that pallor creeps up on [my] forehead together with suffering rife with pain</l>
        <l corresp="7">he has abandoned [us] while we cry, he,</l>
        <l corresp="13">so that [we] shall have the pleasure of preparing a good feast in a rich mansion,</l>
        <l corresp="12">like Paṭṭiṉam with gardens by the Kāviri,</l>
        <l corresp="11">of great name in the middle of long backwaters where flowers unfold,</l>
        <l corresp="10">[belonging to] Kiḷḷi with golden ornaments who desired to take land,</l>
        <l corresp="9">demolishing the shining army of the prosperous Kōcar,</l>
        <l corresp="8">of a fame that shines in the distance for establishing [their] words of truth,</l>
        <l corresp="14">let him easily obtain an excellent treasure,</l>
        <l corresp="24">– he who traversed the desert of lands where the words are different,</l>
        <l corresp="23">that are crossed by stone-glistening difficult ways,</l>
        <l corresp="22cd">little paths within the hills, where,</l>
        <l corresp="15">after the great darkness of the cool season, the time of rains, had left,</l>
        <l corresp="16">on shady mountain sides where long bamboo has come up</l>
        <l corresp="17">so as to resemble the sides of the cheeks of a rutting elephant,</l>
        <l corresp="18">on tops desirable although dislodged when the water crept up,</l>
        <l corresp="19">resembling the striped hide of tiger skins when, to a great clamour</l>
        <l corresp="20">the fragrant blossoms of the kino tree with day[-fresh] flowers were shed [on them],</l>
        <l corresp="21">male monkeys in hordes climb large branches that rise high,</l>
        <l rend="indent6" corresp="22ab">call out [and] leap.</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
